-- title:
--   Frobenius charpoly congruence at the excluded primes ℓ ∤ Np
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N \ge 1$, and let $S_0$ be a finite set of naturals. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a domain that is a discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, with finite residue field, and suppose $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}'$. Let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S_0$ and `heckeULin` for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S_0$ — to $\mathcal{O}'$. Let $k$ be a field, $\psi : k \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}'$ a ring homomorphism, and $\bar\rho$ a [`ResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Residual.html#L22) over $k$: a $2$-dimensional $k$-vector space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ that is trivial on the pointwise stabiliser of some finite-dimensional intermediate field. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals and assume: for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S_0$ and $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ acting on the residue field of $P$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, one has $(\mathrm{charpoly}\,\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma))^{\psi} = X^2 - \overline{\chi(T_\ell)}\,X + \ell$ in $(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}')[X]$. Then the same identity holds for every prime $\ell \ne p$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S_0$, every such $P$ above $\ell$ and every such $\sigma$, with $T_\ell$ taken in `heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`.
--
--   This removes the auxiliary finite exceptional set $S$ from a congruence between the mod-$p$ reduction of a weight-two Hecke eigensystem and a two-dimensional residual Galois representation: the Frobenius characteristic polynomial identity, known outside $S$, is propagated to all primes $\ell \nmid Np$ outside $S_0$. It is the step of the proof of Darmon–Diamond–Taylor's level-lowering lemma that recovers the eigenvalues of the operators $T_\ell$ at the primes discarded from the anemic Hecke algebra, and it feeds the constructions of ring homomorphisms out of Hecke algebras and the bijectivity statement for the local Hecke algebra that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_point_residual_charpoly_frobenius_eq_of_forall_not_mem.lean

